Subject: [PATCH 10874/11362] Record that my planner prompt fix held one
 milestone then failed

On 2026-09-02 I added the two-files-must-agree section to the planner prompt
after the document/YAML divergence happened twice in a day. Milestone 605 came
out 12 and 12 and I reported the fix working. Milestone 606 came out 14 and 4.
The fix is not sufficient and I am recording that rather than leaving the
earlier report standing.

The numbers point away from the prompt. Tasks-proposed over the last eight
milestones runs 4, 9, 4, 4, 4, 7, 12, 4, and every divergence anyone has
measured -- 11 against 4, 13 against 4, and now 14 against 4 -- has a YAML of
exactly four, while the runs producing 7, 9 and 12 include the one measured
clean. A model ignoring an instruction would scatter. A constant 4 looks like
the YAML write being cut short, and no prompt instruction fixes truncation.

I drafted "the YAML is always 4", checked it, and narrowed it: false as a
universal, since 601 and 604 proposed 9 and 7. The claim that survives is that
all three measured divergences had four.

Ten declared tasks, exp6927 through exp6936, have no YAML entry and will never
run. The contract gate caught it correctly and blocked.

Notes an unestablished link deliberately as unestablished: the 606 planner timed
out at 07:35 before succeeding at 08:59, and whether a retried planner truncates
is untested. Records the two experiments that would settle it.

Also records a second defect visible in the same artifact: prior_failure_
validation failed for exp6924 and exp6925, which match archived experiments with
no prior_failures field, and the milestone activated and ran them anyway. The
rerun discipline detected the violation and did not block on it.

